  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Accordion. Objective: one pile. Legal move: top card to 1-left or 3-left if suit or rank matches destination top card.',
    Player: 'Can this card move one left or three left onto a matching suit or rank? If yes, move it and close the gap.',
    objective: 'Compress the entire deck into a single pile. The game is won when all 52 cards are in one pile; the layout is so named because compressing the row resembles closing accordion pleats.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal one card at a time into a row of face-up piles. 2. A top card may move onto the pile immediately to its left or three piles to its left if the destination top card matches suit or rank. 3. After a move, close gaps so piles stay contiguous. 4. Continue moving whenever legal moves exist. 5. Hand ends when no legal moves remain.',
    keyRules: [
      'Moves are always to the left.',
      'A move is legal only when suit or rank matches the destination top card.',
      'The allowed jump distances are exactly 1-left and 3-left.',
    ],
